{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03F0", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-cohomology-modules-abelian-agree}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:726b7d882fa7ca474fd29f1569cd8ed0fc9a96e7dfdd5f692d568c6f38030f0e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma will be superseded by the more general\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:875f0fc92947cdb320cc099df904d0cd93168dacee3394e6e0281516b3e86b47", "unit_id": "tag:03F0:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03F0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}_{ab}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nH^1(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{F}_{ab})\n=\nH^1(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{F})\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$\\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0008": "$\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-h1-mod-ab-agree}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7ac7c446b559df8f22925dc61c2e3837caeb3cfba74b3c7b5fb37cad48ee0bdd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9f375f925e42e5b2834a01c64c2fe0a9984584cc114223e48b289010adf0d923", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of <MATH_0003>-modules on <MATH_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0005> denote the underlying sheaf of abelian\ngroups. Then there is a functorial isomorphism\n<MATH_0006>\nwhere the left hand side is cohomology computed in\n<MATH_0007> and the right hand side\nis cohomology computed in <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:905693dacaf15608c07158aed3135aa773b241f0150429537e9902d2766609e5", "unit_id": "tag:03F2:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03F0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{C}) = \\textit{Mod}(\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}})$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\Ext^1_{\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})}(\\mathcal{O}, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\Ext^1_{\\textit{Mod}(\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}})}(\n\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}}, \\mathcal{F}_{ab}).\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$0 \\to \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{E} \\to \\mathcal{O} \\to 0$", "MATH_0006": "$\\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0007": "$1 : \\underline{\\mathbf{Z}} \\to \\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{E}_{ab}$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n0 \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{F}_{ab} \\ar[r] \\ar@{=}[d] &\n\\mathcal{E}_{ab} \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}} \\ar[r] \\ar[d]^{1} &\n0 \\\\\n0 \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{F} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{E} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{O} \\ar[r] &\n0\n}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$0 \\to \\mathcal{F}_{ab} \\to \\mathcal{E}_{ab} \\to \\underline{\\mathbf{Z}} \\to 0$", "MATH_0011": "$\\textit{Mod}(\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}})$", "MATH_0012": "$\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}}$", "MATH_0014": "$$\n0 \\to \\mathcal{F}_{ab} \\otimes_{\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}}} \\mathcal{O}\n\\to \\mathcal{E}_{ab} \\otimes_{\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}}} \\mathcal{O}\n\\to \\underline{\\mathbf{Z}} \\otimes_{\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}}} \\mathcal{O}\n\\to 0\n$$", "MATH_0015": "$\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}} \\otimes_{\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}}} \\mathcal{O}\n= \\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mu : \\mathcal{F} \\otimes_{\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}}} \\mathcal{O}\n\\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0020": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n0 \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{F}_{ab} \\otimes_{\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}}} \\mathcal{O}\n\\ar[r] \\ar[d]^\\mu &\n\\mathcal{E}_{ab} \\otimes_{\\underline{\\mathbf{Z}}} \\mathcal{O}\n\\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\mathcal{O} \\ar[r] \\ar@{=}[d] &\n0 \\\\\n0 \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{F} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{E} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{O} \\ar[r] &\n0\n}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-h1-extensions}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-flat-tor-zero}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dff4594b89b0ec6156d033315fa156a125c88cc802464b09da90ad7394035a90", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b9eedcc23dede6918ff7994424ea1d3747923b7af2561b1c1ea85352929760e7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> denote the constant sheaf\n<MATH_0002>. As\n<MATH_0003>\nwe may apply\nLemma <REF_0001>\ntwice, and it follows that we have to show\n<MATH_0004>\nSuppose that <MATH_0005>\nis an extension in <MATH_0006>. Then we can use\nthe obvious map of abelian sheaves\n<MATH_0007>\nand pullback to obtain an extension <MATH_0008>, like so:\n<MATH_0009>\nThe converse is a little more fun. Suppose that\n<MATH_0010>\nis an extension in <MATH_0011>.\nSince <MATH_0012> is a flat <MATH_0013>-module\nwe see that the sequence\n<MATH_0014>\nis exact, see\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nOf course\n<MATH_0015>.\nHence we can form the pushout via the (<MATH_0016>-linear) multiplication map\n<MATH_0017> to get an extension of <MATH_0018> by\n<MATH_0019>, like this\n<MATH_0020>\nwhich is the desired extension. We omit the verification that these\nconstructions are mutually inverse.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1e9e01b57cc3e0bad7d53943846fd0e18fe455e2049c6732008937ad1c72859e", "unit_id": "tag:03F2:proof"}
